    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "name": "README.md",
      "kind": "source",
      "source": "# Interactive 3D Wireframe\n\nThis standalone Web64 project renders a perspective wireframe cube with the optimized Bitmap Drawing Runtime.\n\n- `W` / `S` rotate around the X axis (pitch).\n- `A` / `D` rotate around the Y axis (yaw).\n- The included `rotation-matrices.h` is generated by Web64's Matrix generator from the `rotation3d-x` and `rotation3d-y` presets.\n- Each table contains 32 cyclic row-major Q8.8 matrices using column-vector math.\n- Eight cube vertices are transformed and projected into the 320x200 hires bitmap.\n- The 12 edges use `web64_bitmap_line_fast()`. XOR drawing erases the previous wireframe exactly before drawing the updated orientation.\n- The project owns its bitmap, palette, transformed coordinates, and rotation indices; the runtime adds no scene graph or hidden object state.\n\nOpen `bitmap-wireframe-3d.web64proj` in Web64 IDE and run it. Keep keyboard focus on the emulator while using WASD.\n"
    }
  ]
}
